        <h1>Flight Manager Project Overview</h1>
        <h2>1. Quick Overview</h2>
        <p>The Flight Manager is a system designed for reserving airplane tickets and managing flights. It allows users to track past flights along with information regarding the passengers who have traveled.</p>

        <h2>2. Components</h2>
        <p>The Flight Manager consists of two main components: a <strong>Database</strong> for storing flight and reservation data, and a <strong>Web Application</strong> that interfaces with the database.</p>

        <h2>3. Functionality</h2>
        <h3>Users</h3>
        <p>The system operates without requiring user login for ticket reservations. An administrative account is required for managing flights, with an initial single admin having full CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) rights.</p>

        <h3>Flights</h3>
        <p>The system keeps records of flights along with related information, managed only by the administrator. Each flight must include departure and arrival locations, times, aircraft details, and passenger capacities.</p>

        <h3>Reservations</h3>
        <p>Every user can submit a reservation request without logging in, providing information for each passenger. If enough seats are available, confirmation emails are sent upon successful reservations.</p>

        <h2>Team Members</h2>
        <p>Stiliyan Hristov, Konstantin Minchev, Kristian Raykov, Miroslav Nedyalkov</p>

        <h2>Project Goal</h2>
        <p>The goal of the project is to create a web application along with a functioning database using ASP.NET, resulting in a complete Flight Manager application for reserving plane tickets.</p>

        <h2>Technologies Used</h2>
        <p>C#, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, ASP.NET, SQLite</p>

        <h2>Important Dates</h2>
        <p>📅 Start Date: September 24, 2024 | 🏁 End Date: February 28, 2025</p>
